  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (4 of 4).\n\nI added `test/satisfies.test.js` with three tests:\n- **True cases:** versions that should match.\n- **False cases:** versions that should not match.\n- **Invalid input:** bad versions, bad ranges and non-string arguments all return `false` without throwing.\n\nTogether they cover every example table in the spec, including the prerelease rules and ordering.\n\nWhere the spec was silent, I made these choices:\n- **Wildcard order:** a number after a wildcard, as in `1.x.3`, makes the range invalid.\n- **Prerelease on a partial version:** a prerelease tag on a partial version, as in `1.x-beta`, is invalid.\n- **Empty set after `||`:** an empty set, as in `1.0.0 ||`, matches any version, which is how node-semver treats it.\n- **`>*` and `<*`:** these match nothing, while `*`, `>=*`, `<=*` and `=*` match any non-prerelease version.\n- **Leading zeros in prerelease identifiers:** these are accepted, because the spec only restricts leading zeros in MAJOR, MINOR and PATCH.",
